# Interruption $FF, which no site in the ROM requests: it clears the request
# and `songInterruptionPlaying` and plays on (M2RoS bank_004.asm:232). Sent
# mid-earthquake, where `songInterruptionPlaying` is still $0E, so the clear
# shows in the read-back; the quake's song itself carries on. Then an end
# request $03 with nothing to end, which copies the backup back regardless.
# Five seconds.
[songRequest=04]
